<p class="lead">New work arrives at most firms as an email with attachments, a web form, or a phone call. Someone reads it, types the details into the practice system, checks for conflicts, asks for what's missing and sends an engagement letter. Client intake automation does the reading and typing so your team can focus on the decisions.</p>
<h2 id="what-intake-usually-involves">What intake usually involves</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Reading the request and any attached documents.</li>
  <li>Creating the client and the matter or job in your system.</li>
  <li>Checking for duplicates and conflicts.</li>
  <li>Asking the client for missing information.</li>
  <li>Sending an engagement letter or terms for signature.</li>
  <li>Assigning the work to the right person.</li>
</ol>
<h2 id="what-automation-does">What automation does</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Reads the email and attachments and pulls out names, companies, dates, amounts, reference numbers and the type of work.</li>
  <li>Fills the record in your practice or CRM system.</li>
  <li>Flags possible duplicates and conflicts for a person to decide.</li>
  <li>Drafts the follow-up asking for anything missing.</li>
  <li>Prepares the engagement letter and sends it for e-signature through a tool such as <a href="/integrations/docusign">DocuSign</a> once approved.</li>
  <li>Routes the work to the right team member by type, client or workload.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="the-verification-screen">The verification screen</h2>
<p>The key design piece is one screen showing the original email or document on one side and the filled form on the other. Staff check and correct in seconds, and every correction helps tune the system. Nothing goes live without that check.</p>
<h2 id="what-stays-with-your-team">What stays with your team</h2>
<p>Whether to take the client, how to resolve a possible conflict and what to charge stay with people. Automation prepares the decision; it never makes it.</p>
<h2 id="a-real-example">A real example</h2>
<p>For a <a href="/case-studies/flss-legal-process-serving">process serving company</a>, we built intake that reads service requests from emails and PDFs and fills the job fields, with a split-screen verification step. Intake and invoicing became fully automated, with staff checking each job before it goes live. The same pattern works for law, accounting and consulting firms. See our <a href="/solutions/professional-services">professional services page</a>.</p>
